# parts.rules: the functions that name a part of Tier 0's row (tools/parts.c reads it; buster#2874's item 1).
# CLASS|PART|SUBPART|PATTERN. `part`: one of the issue's eight parts. `rest`: in the row, no part the issue lists.
# `out`: a family a compile runs outside the row, which keeps its samples where it is inlined into the row's driver.
# `far`: the rest of the compile. `libc`: libc's samples whose caller the branch stack didn't hold.
# A sample goes to its innermost function with a rule that isn't `far`; a helper inlined into a pass has no rule of its
# own, so the pass takes it. Only then to its innermost function with a `far` rule, so that a front end's helper inlined
# into the row's code is the row's. `^NAME` is for a function compiled out of line: only where it is the chain's symbol.

# --- the stream's decode: Tier 0's passes over the kinds, classes and values, 64 entries at a time
